{
  "version": "workout-types-1",
  "description": "Canonical workout types for workout mode (docs/context-watchdog/WORKOUTS.md). A logged workout is saved under one id; its attributes tell every pipeline what the strap should see. Mirrored in Swift (StrandAnalytics WorkoutTypeCatalog), the edge (_shared/workoutTypes.ts) and SQL (public.workout_types); a parity test pins each to this file. Ids are never renamed or removed: a change is a new catalogue version. sport_name is the label the workout is stored under in the phone's workout table (WorkoutCatalog, cross-platform data) and the existing decoder reads its kind from it: decoder_kind must equal WorkoutKind(sport: sport_name). sport_aliases are the other WorkoutCatalog labels that resolve to the type (manual or imported rows that never had a type).",
  "environments": ["indoor", "outdoor", "either"],
  "locomotions": ["walking", "running", "cycling", "none", "mixed"],
  "efforts": ["light", "moderate", "vigorous", "resistance"],
  "arm_motions": ["swing", "fixed", "varied"],
  "decoder_kinds": ["running", "walking", "cycling", "other"],
  "attributes": {
    "environment": "Where it happens. indoor: no outdoor route, no GPS assumptions; either: both are common.",
    "locomotion": "The body's travel pattern: walking / running / cycling, none for a stationary or floor workout, mixed for several.",
    "effort": "light, moderate, vigorous (cardio load) or resistance (load the strap sees mostly as stillness between sets).",
    "gait_expected": "Gait (walking or running steps) is expected for much of it: ElderNet gait windows inside it are expected, outside such types they are unexpected when locomotion is none or cycling.",
    "arm_motion": "What the wrist or arm does: swing (free arm swing), fixed (hands on bars or handles), varied (changes through the workout, or handrails may be held).",
    "steps_expected": "The strap's step counter is expected to count during it."
  },
